        <body>
            <div xml:id="d377">

                <pb facs="0373" n="303" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg303"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">725.34/17: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Weddell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-08-07T17:00:00-04:00">August 7, 1934—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:13 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>113. This morning the Minister for Foreign Affairs showed me a letter dated today
                    from the Chilean Ambassador here quoting a <pb facs="0374" n="304"
                        xml:id="pg304"/> message from the Chilean Government informing him that in
                    view of the Paraguayan note of recent date self-respect required that Chilean
                    Government withdraw its Minister from Asunción.</p>
                <p>The Minister for Foreign Affairs stated explicitly that he did not consider this
                    a rupture of diplomatic relations but that the entire personnel of the Legation
                    would leave Asunción and that the Argentine Government had agreed to take over
                    the archives and that meanwhile he would continue his efforts to rectify this
                    misunderstanding between the two countries.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Weddell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
